<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fourth Universal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fourth Universal of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a> was the proclamation, dated 22 January 1918, by which the Ukrainian People's Republic declared itself an independent and sovereign state. Issued in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> as Bolshevik forces advanced on the city, it abandoned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a>'s earlier aim of federation with a democratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It allowed the republic to sign a separate peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brest-belarus">Brest-Litovsk</a> in February 1918.</p></div>
